1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,325
A model in a notebook helps nobody. Deploy it behind an API, so an app can ask for predictions.

2
00:00:09,030 --> 00:00:17,130
Watch it in the real world. Data drifts as customers and prices change, so retrain on fresh data.

3
00:00:18,830 --> 00:00:26,305
Write a short model card: what the model is for, the data, the results, the limits, and fairness risks.

4
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:33,450
It helps people use the model wisely, and helps you remember why you built it that way.

5
00:00:35,150 --> 00:00:43,900
Learn Python, pandas and scikit-learn, practise on real datasets, and explain your results in plain language.

6
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:52,025
Your final project, built and evaluated end to end, is your first portfolio piece. Good luck!

